("`${esc(PRESETS[FB.rule].name)}’s rules from h.6, applied unchanged: ${esc(cfg.dir === 'desc' ? 'string 1 highest' : 'string 1 lowest')}, ${esc(MODE_TXT[cfg.mode])}${cfg.mode !== 'tab' ? ', ' + esc(NUM_TXT[cfg.num]) : ''}. A lost numeral is played once; a break between unconnected lines is a hatched gap.${FB.rule === 'hagel' ? (FB.text === 'L' ? ' These are the rules of Hagel’s own files, which follow Laroche’s text: signs that cannot be identified are passed over and each line break is a silence of eight units. On this text they reproduce eleven of his sixteen fragment files exactly; the cards say where he departs. The qualifiers change nothing.' : ' Hagel’s own files follow Laroche’s text rather than Dumbrill’s, so they differ in places from these versions; switch the text to Laroche to compare. The qualifiers change nothing.') : ''}`",
 "`把 ${esc(PRESETS[FB.rule].name)} 在 h.6 上的规则原样套用：${esc(cfg.dir === 'desc' ? '弦 1 最高' : '弦 1 最低')}，${esc(MODE_TXT[cfg.mode])}${cfg.mode !== 'tab' ? '，' + esc(NUM_TXT[cfg.num]) : ''}。缺失的数字按 1 次演奏；不相连的行之间以斜线阴影表示空缺。${FB.rule === 'hagel' ? (FB.text === 'L' ? '这正是 Hagel 自己文件所用的规则，而他的文件依据的是 Laroche 的文本：无法辨认的符号略过不奏，每到换行处留八个单位的静默。用这个文本，他十六个残片文件中有十一个完全吻合；他另作处理的地方，卡片上都有说明。修饰词不改变任何音。' : 'Hagel 自己的文件依据的是 Laroche 而不是 Dumbrill 的文本，所以与这里的版本有些地方不同；把文本切换到 Laroche 即可比较。修饰词不改变任何音。') : ''}`"),
('<div class="card"><span class="kicker">Primaries against secondaries</span><div class="big-row"><div><div class="big">${P}</div><span class="kicker">fourths/fifths</span></div><div><div class="big">${Sx}</div><span class="kicker">thirds/sixths</span></div><div><div class="big">${pct(P, P + Sx)}</div><span class="kicker">primary</span></div></div><p>Dumbrill counts 27% “descending fifths” and 73% “ascending thirds” across the corpus. The fragments here, restorations included, give much the same proportion.</p></div>',
 '<div class="card"><span class="kicker">主音对与次音对之比</span><div class="big-row"><div><div class="big">${P}</div><span class="kicker">四度/五度</span></div><div><div class="big">${Sx}</div><span class="kicker">三度/六度</span></div><div><div class="big">${pct(P, P + Sx)}</div><span class="kicker">主音对</span></div></div><p>Dumbrill 统计全部材料，得出 27% 是“下行五度”，73% 是“上行三度”。这里的残片（连同补出的部分）比例大致相同。</p></div>'),
('<div class="card"><span class="kicker">West’s test: does the second string step?</span><div class="big-row"><div><div class="big">${WS}/${WP}</div><span class="kicker">fragments</span></div><div><div class="big">${h6w.steps}/${h6w.pairs}</div><span class="kicker">h.6</span></div><div><div class="big">${pct(WS + h6w.steps, WP + h6w.pairs)}</div><span class="kicker">together</span></div></div><p>West found 62 of 88 successions (70%) moving to a neighbouring second string, counting 8 and 9 as 1 and 2. This catalogue includes restored terms, which he left out.</p></div>',
 '<div class="card"><span class="kicker">West 的检验：第二根弦是否级进？</span><div class="big-row"><div><div class="big">${WS}/${WP}</div><span class="kicker">残片</span></div><div><div class="big">${h6w.steps}/${h6w.pairs}</div><span class="kicker">h.6</span></div><div><div class="big">${pct(WS + h6w.steps, WP + h6w.pairs)}</div><span class="kicker">合计</span></div></div><p>West 发现 88 次相继中有 62 次（70%）走到相邻的第二根弦（把 8、9 算作 1、2）。本目录包括了他未计入的补出术语。</p></div>'),
('<div class="card"><span class="kicker">Hagel’s test: what do the qualifiers touch?</span><div class="big-row"><div><div class="big">${Q}</div><span class="kicker">qualified terms</span></div><div><div class="big">${QF}</div><span class="kicker">contain string 7 (f)</span></div></div><p>Every qualified term but one contains string 7; the exception, <i>zirte durie</i> on h.30, Hagel rereads as <i>irbute durie</i>. Hence his idea that <i>ašḫuwe</i> marks f raised to f♯, the first step of modulation, and that h.6 uses the simpler style.</p></div>',
 '<div class="card"><span class="kicker">Hagel 的检验：修饰词涉及哪根弦？</span><div class="big-row"><div><div class="big">${Q}</div><span class="kicker">带修饰词的术语</span></div><div><div class="big">${QF}</div><span class="kicker">含弦 7（f）</span></div></div><p>带修饰词的术语除一个外都含弦 7；那个例外是 h.30 上的 <i>zirte durie</i>，Hagel 把它改读为 <i>irbute durie</i>。由此他认为 <i>ašḫuwe</i> 表示把 f 升为 f♯，即转调的第一步，而 h.6 用的是较简单的风格。</p></div>'),
('<div class="card"><span class="kicker">People and tunings</span><p style="margin-top:6px"><b>Composers</b> (TA, “from”): Urḫiya on h.8, h.11 and h.13 (and restored on h.6 by Kilmer); Puḫiya on h.14; Tapšiḫuni on h.15. <b>Scribes</b> (ŠU, “hand”): Ammurabi on h.6, Ipšali on h.12 and h.13. <b>Tuning</b>: only <i>nīd qablim</i> is ever named (h.6, h.7, h.12).</p><p><b>The three 10s</b> stand on h.6 l. 5, h.8 l. 18 and h.10 l. 7. Hagel shows they cannot belong to the same series as 1–5: a reciting note or a fermata.</p></div>',
 '<div class="card"><span class="kicker">人名与调律</span><p style="margin-top:6px"><b>作曲者</b>（TA，“出自”）：h.8、h.11、h.13 上的 Urḫiya（Kilmer 也在 h.6 上补出了他）；h.14 上的 Puḫiya；h.15 上的 Tapšiḫuni。<b>书吏</b>（ŠU，“手”）：h.6 上的 Ammurabi，h.12 和 h.13 上的 Ipšali。<b>调律</b>：提到过名字的只有 <i>nīd qablim</i>（h.6、h.7、h.12）。</p><p><b>三个 10</b> 分别在 h.6 第 5 行、h.8 第 18 行和 h.10 第 7 行。Hagel 指出它们不可能与 1–5 属于同一序列：是一个吟诵音或一个延长记号。</p></div>'),
